notes={
327678:('excluded_routine_linear_algebra','Conjecture 20 in v2, with the preceding corank-one construction. L = M M^T is real symmetric.','Let P be the orthogonal projection onto ker L. Then Lambda = L + P is invertible: it equals L on (ker L)^perp and the identity on ker L. It retains every nonzero eigenvalue and replaces every zero by 1. This works for every symmetric L, independently of unimodularity.','The literal assertion has a standard spectral-theorem proof; no new significant mathematical ingredient. No numerical search needed.','Only a routine bridge is available; no qualifying endpoint attempted.'),
327679:('parked_deep_family','Cyclic lengths, Hamiltonian paths, divisor condition recovered from both source versions.','Literature finds 2025 computational verification and 2026 grid-based constructions; this is the Buratti-Horak-Rosa problem, close to the explicitly warned sequencing family.','No exhaustive path search: known broad verification makes a small sweep uncompetitive, and no new structural mechanism survived.','Need a full new construction or genuinely new forbidden admissible multiset, with verified range and primary 2026 paper body checked first.'),
327771:('excluded_published_solution','Both source versions retrieved; published follow-up Theorem 2 read in anti-vor.txt.','Berikkyzy-Schulte-Young, Anti-van der Waerden numbers of 3-term arithmetic progressions (2017), Theorem 2 explicitly gives aw([3^m],3)=m+2 for m>=1. The m=0 case follows from the no-progression convention.','Published exact full formula subsumes the record.','Zero novelty credit; no computation or Lean investment.'),
327845:('excluded_source_reported_solution','All four source versions retrieved. v4 Section 1.2 explicitly says the behavior conjecture is proved in [17].','Gill-Gillespie-Semeraro, arXiv:1410.4785v3, Theorem E gives primitivity and eventual full alternating/symmetric groupoid. Its point stabilizer yields the requested group, with parity as printed.','The current source already reports subsequent resolution; exact follow-up statement read.','A separate proof-body and groupoid-to-hole semantic audit would be needed for a formal certificate, but cannot earn discovery credit.'),
328204:('parked_deep_after_small_search','Both survey versions retrieved; exact ordered indegree/outdegree hypotheses distinguished from oriented-graph conditions.','All labeled loopless digraphs on 3 and 4 vertices tested: 64 and 4096. Of these 7 and 180 satisfy strong connectivity and both degree alternatives; all are Hamiltonian. See outputs/graphs-small.json. A 2026 H-linkage paper treats asymptotic degree conditions.','Famous structural conjecture; bounded non-finding does not settle it.','Need an exact full theorem beyond asymptotic robust expansion, or a new finite counterexample.'),
328238:('parked_homotopy_source_gap','One source version, Conjecture 5.5 and preceding Lemma 5.4: restriction values through v6, localized motivic Ext, not an ordinary Steenrod Ext computation.','Later eta-local sphere results found, but a proof of Adams differential patterns must not be substituted for the exact restriction-map conjecture.','No meaningful exhaustive finite certificate for the all-generator restriction map; deep algebraic topology and expensive literal semantics.','Need a source-backed uniform computation of the restriction images, and theorem-scope comparison with later motivic work.'),
328312:('excluded_source_refuted','Both versions retrieved; v2 Section 7 Definition 24, Conjecture 14, Theorem 16 and Figure 3 discussion read.','The source itself gives a reduction tree with shifted polynomial t^4 + beta*(-t^2+4*t^3+2*t^4) + beta^2*(t^2+2*t^3+t^4), and explicitly states that it contradicts Kirillov 7(A).','Re-evaluating the source formula or copying its reduction tree earns zero credit.','No new candidate. A formalized copy would still be a known result.'),
328609:('excluded_source_proved','Both versions retrieved; Theorem 1, Lemma 2 and Theorem 3 framework read.','Theorem 1 of the reserved source proves exactly the induced forbidden-poset O(central binomial coefficient) bound for every finite poset. The proof passes to a hypermatrix bound and applies Klazar-Marcus.','Record open status is stale relative even to its own source.','Zero credit; no exhaustive search necessary.'),
328665:('parked_infinite_cardinality','One version, conjecture and Theorems 1-2 with concluding remarks read.','Source obtains covering number at least cf(kappa) through subgroup filtrations, and resolves regular cardinalities, abelian groups and countable cofinality cases.','Remaining singular uncountable cofinality nonabelian case has no small finite countercertificate route.','Need a new all-cardinality partition construction or an infinite-group obstruction, not a finite-group experiment.'),
328757:('excluded_withdrawn_in_later_version','All three versions retrieved. First-column Bruhat conjecture is v1 Conjecture 3.20 and v2 Conjecture 3.19; the conjecture and first-column discussion disappear in v3.','Source v1/v2 call it a combinatorial consequence of the Table Theorem. Current v3 instead develops revised Table/Box results; do not treat the old conjecture as untouched.','Under the binding brief, removal in a later arXiv version is a withdrawal and the route stops.','No discovery credit. Published-version fidelity remains unverified; do not assert a published proof.'),
328806:('parked_existential_connectivity','One version, Conjecture 3 and adjacent discussion read. G-T denotes vertex deletion here. Source records h(1,r)=r+1 and h(2,r)<=2r+1.','An arbitrary proposed finite bound can fail without refuting existence of some h(k,r). Related 2019 nonseparating-tree work concerns a prescribed isomorphism type and minimum degree, so is not substituted.','Finite sweeps would only test candidate bounds; no general mechanism for the all-k existential statement.','Need uniform construction with a proved h(k,r), or an obstruction family with unbounded connectivity.'),
328892:('parked_analytic_and_scope_gap','One version, Section 4 Conjecture 4.1 and Remark 4.2 read.','Source uses an averaged residue occupancy hypothesis for each Q>=N^epsilon and polynomial image of [N]; the MathDB pointwise 0.99 formulation is a related paraphrase. Published larger-sieve machinery and 2026 entropy work do not by themselves prove this exact all-scale inverse theorem.','No finite N computation refutes implicit constants depending on epsilon.','Need a quantitative inverse sieve theorem with bounded degree and height, and precise source-to-record implication.'),
328916:('parked_after_exact_character_search','Both source versions, Definition 1.2, Conjectures 1.7-1.8, Theorem 1.9 and proof structure read. a0 means n mod p, not an assumed part total.','Every partition for 0<=n<=45 and every prime 5<=p<=n+1 was considered. Classes violating sum(parts<a0)<=a0 were tested against p-singular irreducible characters using exact Murnaghan-Nakayama; none was p-vanishing. For p>n all irreducible degrees are prime to p and the small-part inequality is automatically true. Character code crosschecked by orthogonality and sum of degree squares through n=10.','No counterexample. Source Theorem 1.9 equates this apparently small bound with the full p-vanishing classification; this is not a simple small-part lemma.','Need a uniform nonzero p-singular character for every violating partition, or a certified exceptional class beyond the covered range. Full version-of-record body inaccessible via inherited denied publisher route.'),
328950:('excluded_source_proved','All three versions retrieved; Theorem 4 and Corollary 5 and their proof read.','The source proves every planar graph has an equitable partition into k induced forests for every k>=4. This is exactly the requested existence of an absolute c.','No new result: take c=4.','Zero novelty credit.'),
329044:('excluded_prior_refutation_lead','Source Conjecture 6.1 read. Web search of a primary 2020 publisher article reports Ji et al. already gave an infinite family of counterexamples to this exact degree bound.','The later primary article On balanced bipartitions of graphs explicitly states the conjecture and prior refutation. Direct publisher fetch returned 403; it was not retried.','Excluded from investment on an explicit published-refutation report, not on an independently read Ji construction.','Original Ji theorem/proof body remains unread. This is a conservative no-investment disposition, not a full-scope audited prior proof.'),
329252:('excluded_published_obstruction','One source version and Conjecture 1.6 read. Complement convention recovered: constraints are on nonedges of the representation graph. Conca-Welker LSS follow-up Proposition 2.8 and its nonprimality argument read.','In characteristic 0, for d>3 an LSS ideal with a B_d subgraph is not prime. Take d=4 and B4=K4,4 minus a perfect matching; the representation graph is its complement. Deleting all sets of at most 3 vertices verified that complement is 4-connected. Published Proposition 2.8 therefore already contradicts the record.','A direct instantiation of a published obstruction, with a tiny connectivity check; zero credit.','No new endpoint. Do not confuse this with the distinct radicality conjecture in the same source.'),
329400:('parked_geometric_measure','Both versions and published Beer-index paper retrieved. Conjecture 4.3 remains in the arXiv v2, distinct from Theorem 1.3 for simply connected components.','Triangle filling is weaker than simple connectivity. The punctured-square example violates the triangle filling assumption, so cannot refute this record. Finite unions of closed polygons do not capture the full measurable-set quantifiers.','No qualifying construction or uniform measure bound. Paired 329403 is outside this reservation.','Need an absolute linear estimate under triangle filling, or a family with unbounded b(S)/c(S), including measurable visibility and exact geometry.'),
329506:('parked_after_exhaustive_and_recurrence_search','Both arXiv versions and the published EJC paper retrieved; literal inversion definition, Lemma 4.3, Conjecture 4.4 and adjacent bumping discussion read.','Enumerated row-standard tableaux via ordered row subsets with the exact two-clause inversion statistic. Parameters and full coefficient arrays are in tableaux-exhaustive.json and tableaux-extended.json. No violation. Also checked classical Springer polynomial recurrence over the larger grid in tableau-recurrence.json; recurrence agrees with direct counts on every initial enumerated shape but its all-shape semantic bridge is not proved here.','No counterexample or all-scope bijection. Agreement of a recurrence diagnostic cannot be promoted to a literal Lean endpoint.','Need an invertible inversion-preserving tail bumping map, or a proved recurrence bridge and a general polynomial coefficient identity. Source own Lemma 4.3 plus a few unproved bumps is not a complete proof.'),
329553:('parked_analytic_spectral','One arXiv version, Theorem 4 versus Conjecture 6.1 and preceding negative-eigenvalue count read; publisher metadata/abstract checked.','Theorem 4 proves instability of different, nonzero-tail higher branches. Conjecture 6.1 concerns degenerate branches (u_n,0), small negative frequency and n complex quartets. Numerical stability far away from bifurcation does not refute it.','No finite matrix calculation can certify the exact PDE spectrum and all sufficiently small frequencies without semantic approximation bounds.','Need rigorous splitting of embedded eigenvalues for every n and uniform small-frequency control; source negative-index counts are inconclusive.'),
334608:('parked_after_word_search','One arXiv version and the published Integers A61 paper retrieved. Generalized closures and Conjecture 2 (6n) read; the older 4n obstruction is not this record.','Exhaustive depth-9 binary directive tree, both initial antimorphisms and first letter 0 (complements cover first letter 1), plus 500 seeded random and 2600 suffix-automaton local/random trials. Every factor length of the SAM prefixes was checked. Best detailed lower bounds are in word-sam-extended.json. No ratio >=6. Prefix length stopping thresholds may be exceeded by the last closure, explicitly recorded.','Finite prefix factor counts are lower bounds on infinite complexity; non-findings do not establish the conjecture. Related public periodicity theorem does not imply this complexity bound.','Need either an explicit prefix with >=6n distinct factors and a certified closure extension, or a uniform all-directive factor bound. No qualifying endpoint survives.')}
