summary=f'''# r192 research handback

No qualifying new solution and no Lean endpoint. Zero credit is requested. There are {counts['excluded']} conservative exclusions and {counts['parked']} parked records. This is a bounded investigation, not a completed novelty audit or a fully compliant several-hour campaign pass.

## Exact scope and evidence

All 20 reserved corpus lines are preserved byte for byte in raw/, with one-based chunk locations, chunk hashes, raw hashes and UTF-8 statement hashes in extracted.json and results.json. Every arXiv version listed on the live abstract pages was downloaded; outputs/versions.json records hashes and receipts. Relevant primary definitions and claims were read; whole-paper proof audits and every version of record were not completed. Source snippets, later-work searches and dated HTTP responses are retained. No inaccessible body is treated as clearance.

The live Lean Pool /commits/HEAD revision is {R['heads']['leanpool']}. projects.yml and all candidates/ blobs were fetched at that revision. Omega D5/Problems and OpenAI preprints were screened at the recorded live HEADs. Eight spaced GitHub repository searches were made. Generic keyword matches are retained; the screens found no direct prior proof of the three numerical targets, but are not exhaustive proof-body audits. See outputs/registry-screen.json.

## Strongest routes

* **328916, p-vanishing partitions — parked.** Exact Murnaghan-Nakayama tests through n=45 covered {sum(x['violating_classes_tested'] for x in pv):,} pairs of a prime and a class violating the inequality, with no counterexample. All partitions and relevant primes were generated, and every violating class was rejected by at least one nonzero p-singular character. Character-table orthogonality was independently checked through n=10. The remaining uniform character-existence lemma is equivalent to the full classification in source Theorem 1.9. No significant proof was found.
* **329506, tail-end tableau inversions — parked.** Direct initial enumeration covered {len(tw)} parameter pairs, including (m,n)=(4,3),(5,2). Full enumerators and any completed extended cases are saved. A second recurrence sweep covered {len(tr['rows'])} parameter pairs, with m<=8, n<=12, mn<=60 and binomial(m+n,m)<=30000. Every tested tail identity held. The classical recurrence matches the direct small cases, but its semantic bridge and an all-parameter coefficient proof remain open in this lane.
* **334608, pseudostandard complexity — parked.** All 131,072 depth-9 directive leaves with first letter 0 and either initial antimorphism were tested; complement symmetry covers initial 1. Additional random/local searches checked all factor lengths by a suffix automaton. Best observed ratio was {word['best'][0]:.12f}; the exact directive, factor length and prefix size are saved. No value reached 6. These are finite-prefix lower bounds, not upper bounds for infinite languages. Both SAM counts and closure minimality were independently crosschecked.

## Exclusions and other dispositions

327771 is covered by the published exact anti-van der Waerden formula; 327845 is reported resolved by its latest source and has an exact follow-up; 328312 is refuted by its own source; 328609 and 328950 are proved by their own sources. The first-column Bruhat conjecture 328757 was removed in v3 and is stopped under the binding withdrawal rule. The 329044 published-refutation report is strong enough to avoid investment, but the original refutation body remains unread. The LSS obstruction B4 already refutes 329252 via Conca-Welker Proposition 2.8; its complement connectivity was independently checked. The spectral-projection proof of literal 327678 is routine and uncreditable. Deep, infinite-cardinality, analytic and existential-connectivity records remain parked with explicit gaps in results.json.

## Limits and reproducibility

All writes are lane local. No git, browser tabs, accounts, external messages, uploads or child agents. Computational commands use scripts/limited.py: two-CPU affinity, CPU 120 s, wall 140 s, process-group RSS watchdog 6 GiB, MALLOC_ARENA_MAX=2; full logs and sampled RSS are retained. No Lean was run. The unavailable g++ compile attempt is recorded; Python implementations were used. One bookkeeping error briefly overlapped the low-memory network acquisition process with the random word process; both finished, neither approached the RSS cap. Subsequent expensive work was serialized. This deviation is disclosed rather than claiming perfect scheduling compliance.

Every HTTP receipt is retained without overwriting. TLS verification remained enabled. Inherited denied hosts were avoided; the new TandF 403 was recorded and not retried. Two exploratory follow-up URLs were less precisely identified than appropriate (the unrelated supersimple 1510 paper and a guessed Jordan DOI); they are not used to support a disposition. The exact supersimple reference 1410.4785 was then retrieved from the source bibliography. No code from downloads was executed. Published-version checks remain incomplete for several parked records.

Reproduction: run each numerical script under scripts/limited.py with a fresh log name; output files may be regenerated, HTTP receipts must never be overwritten. outputs/algorithm-verification.json gives crosschecks. Numerical checks are diagnostics, not formal proofs. No source or current public registry non-match establishes mathematical novelty.

Files: results.json (exactly 20 keyed entries), CANDIDATE.md, outputs/registry-screen.json, outputs/http-receipts.json, outputs/versions.json, raw/, sources/, scripts/, logs/.
'''
